{"name":"Sakura Nezu","hex":"#e8dfe4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sakura","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Japanese) cherry tree","cherry blossom (blossom of the Japanese cherry tree)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sakura"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry blossom","blocks":[{"text":"The cherry blossom, or sakura, is the flower of trees in Prunus subgenus Cerasus. Sakura usually refers to flowers of ornamental cherry trees, such as cultivars of Prunus serrulata, not trees grown for their fruit. Cherry blossoms have been described as having a vanilla-like smell, which is mainly attributed to coumarin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg/330px-Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_blossom"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg/500px-Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg/1280px-Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg/500px-Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prunus speciosa (Oshima cherry), a species of cherry tree that has given rise to many cultivar